    <node id="n_hannah_topping_68d674def568">
      <data key="d3">Hannah Topping</data>
      <data key="d4">CHARACTER</data>
      <data key="d5">Formerly in service at the Deanery, portrayed by Miss Laura Linden. | A buxom, fresh-looking young woman in a print gown, engaged in cooking while singing gayly. She is married to Noah Topping and was formerly cook at the Deanery for seven years. | A character in the play, formerly Miss Hevans, now married to Noah Topping, the Head Constable at St. Marvells. | Wife of Noah Topping, a police constable's wife. | Wife of Noah Topping, referred to as 'Annah by Blore. | A character who is the wife of the Constable and former servant of the Dean. | A woman who is helping the Dean, possibly a former servant, now married to Noah Topping. | A servant or former servant at the Deanery, married to Noah Topping for eight weeks. | A woman who is Noah Topping's wife and cooks for the Dean. | The wife of Noah Topping, who cooks for the Dean. | Noah's wife, who made the Dean's acquaintance through the wicket and serves him a meal. | Wife of Noah, works at the police station. | A person who speaks to Georgiana and Sir Tristram. | Woman who arranged for the Dean's escape. | A woman who kneels at Georgiana's feet and says the Dean is the sweetest man in Durnshire. | Wife of Noah Topping, who tries to restrain him. | Noah's wife, formerly Hannah Evans, an excellent cook under the Dean's roof.</data>
      <data key="d6">["Formerly in service at the Deanery, portrayed by Miss Laura Linden.","A buxom, fresh-looking young woman in a print gown, engaged in cooking while singing gayly. She is married to Noah Topping and was formerly cook at the Deanery for seven years.","A character in the play, formerly Miss Hevans, now married to Noah Topping, the Head Constable at St. Marvells.","Wife of Noah Topping, a police constable's wife.","Wife of Noah Topping, referred to as 'Annah by Blore.","A character who is the wife of the Constable and former servant of the Dean.","A woman who is helping the Dean, possibly a former servant, now married to Noah Topping.","A servant or former servant at the Deanery, married to Noah Topping for eight weeks.","A woman who is Noah Topping's wife and cooks for the Dean.","The wife of Noah Topping, who cooks for the Dean.","Noah's wife, who made the Dean's acquaintance through the wicket and serves him a meal.","Wife of Noah, works at the police station.","A person who speaks to Georgiana and Sir Tristram.","Woman who arranged for the Dean's escape.","A woman who kneels at Georgiana's feet and says the Dean is the sweetest man in Durnshire.","Wife of Noah Topping, who tries to restrain him.","Noah's wife, formerly Hannah Evans, an excellent cook under the Dean's roof."]</data>
      <data key="d7">["Annah","HANNAH","Hannah","Hannah Evans","Miss Hevans","Mrs. Topping"]</data>
      <data key="d8">["dd_cast_c0001","dd_act03s01_c0001","dd_act03s01_c0002","dd_act03s01_c0003","dd_act03s01_c0004","dd_act03s01_c0005","dd_act03s01_c0006","dd_act03s01_c0007","dd_act03s01_c0008","dd_act03s01_c0009","dd_act03s01_c0010","dd_act03s01_c0011","dd_act03s01_c0012","dd_act03s01_c0013","dd_act03s02_c0009","dd_act03s02_c0010"]</data>
