    <node id="n_major_tarver_6a2225fc8ba8">
      <data key="d3">Major Tarver</data>
      <data key="d4">CHARACTER</data>
      <data key="d5">A major in the --th Hussars, quartered at Durnstone, near St. Marvell's, portrayed by Mr. F. Kerr. | An officer of the Hussars who proposed the plan to attend the Fancy Dress Masked Ball and is paying attention to Salome. | A major who promised to get the dresses made in London and initially offered to pay for them. | A middle-aged, tall, angular officer with a thin face, yellow complexion, and red eyes. | A middle-aged, tall, angular officer with a thin face, yellow complexion, and red eyes, who suffers from alternating excitement and depression. | Major Tarver, army man, friend of Darbey. | A character in the play, addressed as Major, who is invited to dinner and plans to dress as Charles the First. | A major who enters pale and haggard, suffering from indigestion. | A character who is excited to sing, has his music in his overcoat pocket, and later discovers his music roll is empty. | A character who glares at DARBEY and wants to garrote him with his bass string. | A man present, refuses to lend his boots to Georgiana. | Major Tarver, a guest at the Deanery. | A man dressed as a Cavalier, carrying a carriage umbrella. | A man mentioned by Salome, whose nose is inclined to pink. | A man addressed as Field-Marshal, who is with Darbey at the Swan Inn ruins. | A Major who enters with Mr. Darbey, dressed for the Races, and looks extremely weakly. | A character who proposes to Salome and is accepted. | A character pulled by Salome to take cuttings in the conservatory. | A character mentioned as sitting with Salome in the conservatory. | Sitting on the hot pipes in the conservatory with Salome. | Gallant gentleman who proposed to Salome. | A character who enters with the Dean and later goes into the Library.</data>
      <data key="d6">["A major in the --th Hussars, quartered at Durnstone, near St. Marvell's, portrayed by Mr. F. Kerr.","An officer of the Hussars who proposed the plan to attend the Fancy Dress Masked Ball and is paying attention to Salome.","A major who promised to get the dresses made in London and initially offered to pay for them.","A middle-aged, tall, angular officer with a thin face, yellow complexion, and red eyes.","A middle-aged, tall, angular officer with a thin face, yellow complexion, and red eyes, who suffers from alternating excitement and depression.","Major Tarver, army man, friend of Darbey.","A character in the play, addressed as Major, who is invited to dinner and plans to dress as Charles the First.","A major who enters pale and haggard, suffering from indigestion.","A character who is excited to sing, has his music in his overcoat pocket, and later discovers his music roll is empty.","A character who glares at DARBEY and wants to garrote him with his bass string.","A man present, refuses to lend his boots to Georgiana.","Major Tarver, a guest at the Deanery.","A man dressed as a Cavalier, carrying a carriage umbrella.","A man mentioned by Salome, whose nose is inclined to pink.","A man addressed as Field-Marshal, who is with Darbey at the Swan Inn ruins.","A Major who enters with Mr. Darbey, dressed for the Races, and looks extremely weakly.","A character who proposes to Salome and is accepted.","A character pulled by Salome to take cuttings in the conservatory.","A character mentioned as sitting with Salome in the conservatory.","Sitting on the hot pipes in the conservatory with Salome.","Gallant gentleman who proposed to Salome.","A character who enters with the Dean and later goes into the Library."]</data>
      <data key="d7">["Gerald Tarver","Major","MAJOR TARVER","TARVER","Tarver"]</data>
