    <node id="n_noah_topping_717d5331d0ac">
      <data key="d3">Noah Topping</data>
      <data key="d4">CHARACTER</data>
      <data key="d5">A character in Dandy Dick, suggested by a rural constable of a village adjacent to Brighton. | Constable at St. Marvell's, portrayed by Mr. W. H. Denny. | A constable who is going to sit up with Hatcham for company. | A policeman, husband of Hannah, referred to as Noah Topping. He is in a rough, country voice and is about to drive a prisoner to Durnstone. | Head Constable at St. Marvells, husband of Hannah, referred to as Noah. | A rural Police Constable, husband of Hannah. | Husband of Hannah, a police officer with a truncheon and handcuffs. | A character who instructs Hannah to open the oven door and leaves into the street. | The husband of Hannah, who is going to take the Dean to Durnstone. | Hannah's husband of eight weeks, who will drive the Dean to Durnstone. | A constable who is Hannah's husband and enters through the window. | The constable husband of Hannah, referred to as Noahry by Hannah. | A police officer in St. Marvells, married to Hannah, and concerned about his wife's interactions with the Dean. | Man in charge at the police station, husband of Hannah. | A person taking down a description of the Dean, described as a shrewd experienced man. | Constable who took the man in the Deanery Stables last night. | A constable who arrests the Dean for trespassing and alienating his wife's affections. | Noah Topping, husband of Hannah, who accuses the Dean of being the man who alienated his wife's affections. | A constable who confronts the Dean, believing him to be the man who alienated his wife's affections.</data>
      <data key="d6">["A character in Dandy Dick, suggested by a rural constable of a village adjacent to Brighton.","Constable at St. Marvell's, portrayed by Mr. W. H. Denny.","A constable who is going to sit up with Hatcham for company.","A policeman, husband of Hannah, referred to as Noah Topping. He is in a rough, country voice and is about to drive a prisoner to Durnstone.","Head Constable at St. Marvells, husband of Hannah, referred to as Noah.","A rural Police Constable, husband of Hannah.","Husband of Hannah, a police officer with a truncheon and handcuffs.","A character who instructs Hannah to open the oven door and leaves into the street.","The husband of Hannah, who is going to take the Dean to Durnstone.","Hannah's husband of eight weeks, who will drive the Dean to Durnstone.","A constable who is Hannah's husband and enters through the window.","The constable husband of Hannah, referred to as Noahry by Hannah.","A police officer in St. Marvells, married to Hannah, and concerned about his wife's interactions with the Dean.","Man in charge at the police station, husband of Hannah.","A person taking down a description of the Dean, described as a shrewd experienced man.","Constable who took the man in the Deanery Stables last night.","A constable who arrests the Dean for trespassing and alienating his wife's affections.","Noah Topping, husband of Hannah, who accuses the Dean of being the man who alienated his wife's affections.","A constable who confronts the Dean, believing him to be the man who alienated his wife's affections."]</data>
      <data key="d7">["Mr. Topping","NOAH","Noah","NOAH TOPPING","Noahry","the Constable"]</data>
      <data key="d8">["dd_prod_c0001","dd_cast_c0001","dd_act02_c0007","dd_act03s01_c0001","dd_act03s01_c0002","dd_act03s01_c0003","dd_act03s01_c0004","dd_act03s01_c0005","dd_act03s01_c0007","dd_act03s01_c0008","dd_act03s01_c0009","dd_act03s01_c0010","dd_act03s01_c0011","dd_act03s01_c0012","dd_act03s01_c0013","dd_act03s02_c0009","dd_act03s02_c0010"]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="n_nugent_darbey_aff8668f3a6d">
      <data key="d3">Nugent Darbey</data>
      <data key="d4">CHARACTER</data>
      <data key="d5">Quartered at Durnstone, near St. Marvell's, portrayed by Mr. H. Eversfield. | A lieutenant in the Hussars, described as a small officer, who is impressed by Sheba. | A mere boy, but with a pompous, patronizing manner. | A young officer with a pompous, patronizing manner, who is a visitor. | Army man, friend of Major Tarver. | A character in the play, invited to dinner, who suggests the idea of Charles the Martyr. | A character who enters through the Library, patronizing the Dean. | A character who has brought his violin and plays it, accompanied by Sheba. | A character who plays an instrument and is compared to Joachim by his mother. | A man present, Sheba clings to him. | Mr. Darbey, a guest at the Deanery; invites the Dean to visit. | A character who returns to retrieve his violin and leaves with dignity. | A man dressed as a Cavalier, one of the two men who arrive. | A man mentioned by Sheba, whom she hates. | A man with Tarver, guarding the ruins of the Swan Inn. | A man who enters with Major Tarver, dressed for the Races, and supports Tarver. | A character who tells a story about the Doctor's examination of the Major and later proposes to Sheba. | A character who comments on the situation and leaves quickly. | A character mentioned by Sheba as someone she wants to be with. | Mentioned by Sheba as needing a place to go. | Gallant gentleman who proposed to Sheba. | A character who sits in an arm-chair with Sheba on the arm and later stands behind Sheba at the piano.</data>
      <data key="d6">["Quartered at Durnstone, near St. Marvell's, portrayed by Mr. H. Eversfield.","A lieutenant in the Hussars, described as a small officer, who is impressed by Sheba.","A mere boy, but with a pompous, patronizing manner.","A young officer with a pompous, patronizing manner, who is a visitor.","Army man, friend of Major Tarver.","A character in the play, invited to dinner, who suggests the idea of Charles the Martyr.","A character who enters through the Library, patronizing the Dean.","A character who has brought his violin and plays it, accompanied by Sheba.","A character who plays an instrument and is compared to Joachim by his mother.","A man present, Sheba clings to him.","Mr. Darbey, a guest at the Deanery; invites the Dean to visit.","A character who returns to retrieve his violin and leaves with dignity.","A man dressed as a Cavalier, one of the two men who arrive.","A man mentioned by Sheba, whom she hates.","A man with Tarver, guarding the ruins of the Swan Inn.","A man who enters with Major Tarver, dressed for the Races, and supports Tarver.","A character who tells a story about the Doctor's examination of the Major and later proposes to Sheba.","A character who comments on the situation and leaves quickly.","A character mentioned by Sheba as someone she wants to be with.","Mentioned by Sheba as needing a place to go.","Gallant gentleman who proposed to Sheba.","A character who sits in an arm-chair with Sheba on the arm and later stands behind Sheba at the piano."]</data>
      <data key="d7">["DARBEY","Darbey","MR. DARBEY","Mr. Darbey"]</data>
