    <node id="n_salome_jedd_4164bffbc566">
      <data key="d3">Salome Jedd</data>
      <data key="d4">CHARACTER</data>
      <data key="d5">One of the Dean's daughters, portrayed by Miss Marie Lewes. | A tall, handsome, dark girl of about three-and-twenty, sister of Sheba, daughter of the Dean of St. Marvells. | A character in the play, sister of Sheba, who receives an account for fancy dresses. | A daughter of the Dean, referred to as Miss Salome. | A young woman, sister of Sheba, who is startled by the visitors and concerned about Major Tarver's health. | Daughter of the Dean, sister of Sheba. | Daughter of the Dean, sister of Sheba, who mentions the leg of mutton and admires Tarver's costume idea. | Daughter of the Dean, sister of Sheba, reads the newspaper article about the Restoration Fund. | Daughter of the Dean. | Daughter of the Dean and niece of Georgiana Tidman. | A young woman, daughter of the Dean, sister of Sheba. | A character in the play, niece of the Dean and daughter of Georgiana. | A character in the play, daughter of the Dean. | Niece of Georgiana, sister of Sheba; she and Sheba owe forty pounds unknown to their father. | A young woman who, along with Sheba, owes forty pounds, nineteen shillings unknown to their father and seeks to win money by betting on Dandy Dick. | Niece of Georgiana, lolling on the settee. | A character who discusses a plan to leave the house at night with Sheba. | A character who interacts with Tarver and sits beside him. | A character who hopes her ball-dress will drive other women mad. | A young woman present during the fire, clings to Tarver. | A character who enters in a fancy dress and is upset about no ball. | A young woman in fancy dress, upset about the cancelled ball. | A young woman, niece of Georgiana, who pleads for Tarver and Darbey. | A daughter of the Dean, present in the Morning Room at the Deanery. | A character who is proposed to by Major Tarver and is concerned about her father being out all night. | A character in the play who expresses concern about her Papa. | A character mentioned as sitting with Major Tarver in the conservatory. | Daughter of the Dean, sister of Sheba, and niece of Georgiana. | A girl who enters and listens, later hides behind window curtains. | Daughter of the Dean, proposed to by Major Tarver. | A character who enters with the Dean and later goes into the Library.</data>
      <data key="d6">["One of the Dean's daughters, portrayed by Miss Marie Lewes.","A tall, handsome, dark girl of about three-and-twenty, sister of Sheba, daughter of the Dean of St. Marvells.","A character in the play, sister of Sheba, who receives an account for fancy dresses.","A daughter of the Dean, referred to as Miss Salome.","A young woman, sister of Sheba, who is startled by the visitors and concerned about Major Tarver's health.","Daughter of the Dean, sister of Sheba.","Daughter of the Dean, sister of Sheba, who mentions the leg of mutton and admires Tarver's costume idea.","Daughter of the Dean, sister of Sheba, reads the newspaper article about the Restoration Fund.","Daughter of the Dean.","Daughter of the Dean and niece of Georgiana Tidman.","A young woman, daughter of the Dean, sister of Sheba.","A character in the play, niece of the Dean and daughter of Georgiana.","A character in the play, daughter of the Dean.","Niece of Georgiana, sister of Sheba; she and Sheba owe forty pounds unknown to their father.","A young woman who, along with Sheba, owes forty pounds, nineteen shillings unknown to their father and seeks to win money by betting on Dandy Dick.","Niece of Georgiana, lolling on the settee.","A character who discusses a plan to leave the house at night with Sheba.","A character who interacts with Tarver and sits beside him.","A character who hopes her ball-dress will drive other women mad.","A young woman present during the fire, clings to Tarver.","A character who enters in a fancy dress and is upset about no ball.","A young woman in fancy dress, upset about the cancelled ball.","A young woman, niece of Georgiana, who pleads for Tarver and Darbey.","A daughter of the Dean, present in the Morning Room at the Deanery.","A character who is proposed to by Major Tarver and is concerned about her father being out all night.","A character in the play who expresses concern about her Papa.","A character mentioned as sitting with Major Tarver in the 