    <node id="n_sheba_jedd_77083cdc8c2f">
      <data key="d3">Sheba Jedd</data>
      <data key="d4">CHARACTER</data>
      <data key="d5">One of the Dean's daughters, portrayed by Miss Norreys. | A fair little girl of about seventeen, sister of Salome, daughter of the Dean of St. Marvells. | A character in the play, sister of Salome, who reacts to the dress account. | A daughter of the Dean, referred to as Miss Sheba. | A young woman, sister of Salome, who interacts with Mr. Darbey and is involved in the costume arrangements. | Daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome. | Daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome, who mentions custards and is asked to watch the Dean carve fairly. | Daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome, upset about lack of new clothing. | Daughter of the Dean. | Daughter of the Dean and niece of Georgiana Tidman. | A young woman, daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome. | A character in the play, niece of the Dean and daughter of Georgiana. | A character in the play, daughter of the Dean. | Niece of Georgiana, sister of Salome; she and Salome owe forty pounds unknown to their father. | A young woman who, along with Salome, owes forty pounds unknown to their father and seeks to win money by betting on Dandy Dick. | Niece of Georgiana, playing the piano. | A character who discusses a plan to leave the house at night with Salome. | A character who mentions Darbey's violin and accompanies him on the piano. | A character who accompanies DARBEY on an instrument and is concerned about her father being in the way. | A young woman present during the fire, clings to Darbey. | A character whose little cot is still standing in the old nursery. | A character who enters in a fancy dress and is upset about no ball. | A young woman in fancy dress, upset about the cancelled ball. | A young woman, niece of Georgiana, who pleads for Tarver and Darbey. | A daughter of the Dean, present in the Morning Room at the Deanery. | A character who is proposed to by Darbey and asks for time to consider. | A character who announces Aunt Georgiana's arrival and decides to follow Mr. Darbey. | A character in the play, daughter of the Dean, who is looking for a place to go with Mr. Darbey. | Daughter of the Dean, referred to as Papsey by Sheba. | Daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome, and niece of Georgiana. | A girl who enters and listens, later hides behind window curtains. | Daughter of the Dean, proposed to by Mr. Darbey. | A character who sits on the arm of Darbey's chair and later plays the piano.</data>
      <data key="d6">["One of the Dean's daughters, portrayed by Miss Norreys.","A fair little girl of about seventeen, sister of Salome, daughter of the Dean of St. Marvells.","A character in the play, sister of Salome, who reacts to the dress account.","A daughter of the Dean, referred to as Miss Sheba.","A young woman, sister of Salome, who interacts with Mr. Darbey and is involved in the costume arrangements.","Daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome.","Daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome, who mentions custards and is asked to watch the Dean carve fairly.","Daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome, upset about lack of new clothing.","Daughter of the Dean.","Daughter of the Dean and niece of Georgiana Tidman.","A young woman, daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome.","A character in the play, niece of the Dean and daughter of Georgiana.","A character in the play, daughter of the Dean.","Niece of Georgiana, sister of Salome; she and Salome owe forty pounds unknown to their father.","A young woman who, along with Salome, owes forty pounds unknown to their father and seeks to win money by betting on Dandy Dick.","Niece of Georgiana, playing the piano.","A character who discusses a plan to leave the house at night with Salome.","A character who mentions Darbey's violin and accompanies him on the piano.","A character who accompanies DARBEY on an instrument and is concerned about her father being in the way.","A young woman present during the fire, clings to Darbey.","A character whose little cot is still standing in the old nursery.","A character who enters in a fancy dress and is upset about no ball.","A young woman in fancy dress, upset about the cancelled ball.","A young woman, niece of Georgiana, who pleads for Tarver and Darbey.","A daughter of the Dean, present in the Morning Room at the Deanery.","A character who is proposed to by Darbey and asks for time to consider.","A character who announces Aunt Georgiana's arrival and decides to follow Mr. Darbey.","A character in the play, daughter of the Dean, who is looking for a place to go with Mr. Darbey.","Daughter of the Dean, referred to as Papsey by Sheba.","Daughter of the Dean, sister of Salome, and niece of Georgiana.","A girl who enters and listens, later hides behind window curtains.","Daughter of the Dean, proposed to by Mr. Darbey.","A character who sits on the arm of Darbey's chair and later plays the piano."]</data>
