    <node id="n_sir_tristram_mardon_d545f9da176d">
      <data key="d3">Sir Tristram Mardon</data>
      <data key="d4">CHARACTER</data>
      <data key="d5">A baronet, portrayed by Mr. Edmund Maurice. | A well-preserved man of about fifty, a bachelor, and old Oxford friend of the Dean. | A bachelor who was jilted years ago and is in St. Marvells for the races. | A character in the play, referred to as Mardon and Tris, who is a friend of the Dean from Oxford. | A character in the play, referred to as 'Tris' by Georgiana. | Referred to as Tris and partner; he is involved with Dandy Dick and the Durnstone Handicap. | A man who rushes in with news about the horse, referred to as Tris Mardon. | Owner of Dandy Dick, the horse. | A character who is concerned about the horse Dandy and discusses the fire with Hatcham. | A character who is staying at the Deanery and is put to bed in the nursery. | A character who enters quietly, smoking and carrying a lighted candle, and later encounters Georgiana. | A character in the play who interacts with Georgiana and offers to swap halves of the horse Dandy. | A character who takes a candlestick and leaves the room with others to watch. | A man called Tris, who twists Tarver's wig and is involved with the stable. | A gentleman who visits the police station with Georgiana, dressed for the race-course. | A gentleman accompanying Georgiana to the police station. | Friend of Augustin Jedd, referred to as his friend. | Owner of the horse stabled at the Deanery. | A man who tells Noah to release the Dean and asks the Dean for the key to his handcuffs. | A character who helps carry the Dean and participates in the rescue. | A character in the play who assists Georgiana in the rescue. | A character in the play, also called Tris, who owns the horse Dandy Dick and is in love with Georgiana. | Present in the room with Aunt, goes out at the window following Hatcham. | Friend and future relative of the Dean, and owner of one-half of Dandy Dick. | Owner of one-half of Dandy Dick. | Present at the Deanery, tells Noah to go away. | A character who questions Hatcham about the man secured in the stable. | A character in the play who speaks to the Dean.</data>
      <data key="d6">["A baronet, portrayed by Mr. Edmund Maurice.","A well-preserved man of about fifty, a bachelor, and old Oxford friend of the Dean.","A bachelor who was jilted years ago and is in St. Marvells for the races.","A character in the play, referred to as Mardon and Tris, who is a friend of the Dean from Oxford.","A character in the play, referred to as 'Tris' by Georgiana.","Referred to as Tris and partner; he is involved with Dandy Dick and the Durnstone Handicap.","A man who rushes in with news about the horse, referred to as Tris Mardon.","Owner of Dandy Dick, the horse.","A character who is concerned about the horse Dandy and discusses the fire with Hatcham.","A character who is staying at the Deanery and is put to bed in the nursery.","A character who enters quietly, smoking and carrying a lighted candle, and later encounters Georgiana.","A character in the play who interacts with Georgiana and offers to swap halves of the horse Dandy.","A character who takes a candlestick and leaves the room with others to watch.","A man called Tris, who twists Tarver's wig and is involved with the stable.","A gentleman who visits the police station with Georgiana, dressed for the race-course.","A gentleman accompanying Georgiana to the police station.","Friend of Augustin Jedd, referred to as his friend.","Owner of the horse stabled at the Deanery.","A man who tells Noah to release the Dean and asks the Dean for the key to his handcuffs.","A character who helps carry the Dean and participates in the rescue.","A character in the play who assists Georgiana in the rescue.","A character in the play, also called Tris, who owns the horse Dandy Dick and is in love with Georgiana.","Present in the room with Aunt, goes out at the window following Hatcham.","Friend and future relative of the Dean, and owner of one-half of Dandy Dick.","Owner of one-half of Dandy Dick.","Present at the Deanery, tells Noah to go away.","A character who questions Hatcham about the man secured in the stable.","A character in the play who speaks to the Dean."]</data>
      <data key="d7">["Mardon","SIR TRISTRAM","Sir Tristram","Sir Tristram Mardon, Bart","Tris","Tris Mardon","Tristram"]</data>
      <data key="d8">["dd_cast_c0001","dd_act01_c0012","dd_act01_c0013","dd_act01_c0014","dd_act01_c0015","dd_act01_c0016","dd_act02_c0005","dd_act02_c0006","dd_act02_c0007","dd_act02_c0008","dd_act02_c0014","dd_act02_c0015","dd_act02_c0016","dd_act02_c0017","dd_act03s01_c0009","dd_act03s01_c0010","dd_act03s01_c0011","dd_act03s01_c0012","dd_act03s01_c0013","dd_act03s02_c0003","dd_act03s02_c0004","dd_act03s02_c0005","dd_act03s02_c0006","dd_act03s02_c0007","dd_act03s02_c0008","dd_act03s02_c0009","dd_act03s02_c0010","dd_act03s02_c0011"]</data>
